      "used_by_eos_records": ["beryllium_hcp_dewaele_2019_mao_vinet", "beryllium_hcp_dewaele_2019_dor_vinet"],
      "notes": "The APS version of record is the numerical authority. Its 24.6 GPa Be+He_3 row prints a=2.162 A; the earlier OSTI accepted manuscript prints a=2.262 A. Both tokens are preserved explicitly, and the fit uses only the version-of-record column. Atomic volume is derived as sqrt(3)*a^2*c/4 per atom. Dewaele (2019), Section 4, confirms that the original Be pressures use the Dorogokupets--Oganov scale."
    }
